'''Werewolf''' is a {{Mythical}} [[mutation]] of [[Tiger]]. 

Werewolf allows the user to transform into an anthropomorphic wolf, granting them aggressive and powerful attacks as well as enhanced speed, agility, and offense.  Compared to [[Tiger]], it has reduced speed, accuracy, and hitboxes, in exchange for excellent offensive and self-sustain capabilities. This is largely due to its '''[Z] Finger Revolver''' ability, which deals spread damage, its passive life leech while transformed, and its Blazing Form, which heals 30% of the user's maximum health upon activation and fully restores the user’s [[health]] upon defeating another player.

Werewolf also possesses a custom cutscene on its '''[C] Afterimage Assault'''. The move has less knockback and a wider hitbox (albeit slightly shorter) than its [[Tiger]] counterpart, making it good for PvP.

==Obtainment==
As a [[Mutation]], Werewolf has different obtainment methods compared to ordinary [[Blox Fruits]]. Players are able to obtain it by:
* Rolling it through the limited-time [[Halloween Gacha Dealer|Halloween Gacha]].
* Buying it with{{Robux|1,500}} from the mutation section of the [[Tiger]] fruit. (Must own [[Permanent Blox Fruits|Permanent]] [[Tiger]] first).
* Buying the [[shop|Hunter Bundle]] during the 2025 Halloween event.
* [[Trading]].
* Randomly spawning across the map like how normal [[Blox Fruits]] spawn during the [[Events|2025 Halloween event.]]
* Small chance by defeating the [[Unbound Werewolf|Werewolf Boss]] during the hourly [[Trick or Treating|Trick or Treat]] event.

