== Trivia ==
* Werewolf is the first [[Mutations|Mutation]] added to the game.
** This is evident in the fact that the moves share names with [[Tiger]] ,while newer ones (like [[Empyrean]]) do not. And it only really has 1 'mutated' move.
*** '''[F] Body Flicker''' barely has a difference, simply having a slightly altered animation, and lowered knockback.
* Upon defeating players in Blazing Form, the user’s health fully regenerates.
* The user lets out a loud howl after 'devouring' an enemy in the Blazing Form. This does have an animation, but it is extremely short and is barely noticable.
* Transforming disables the user's ability to sit down on a [[boats|boat]] and/or [[Shipwright|repair]] it.
* Werewolf's {{Ability|V}} removes fog effects for the duration of the roar.
** This can be very useful in areas like the [[Mirage Island]], since it has a low cooldown, and illuminates the area, making the user finding [[Advanced Fruit Dealer]] or [[Blue Gear]] more easier.
** Sometimes, the user will be abruptly teleported to a nearby location after briefly teleporting to the [[sea]], rather than their exact position prior to the glitch happening. When at [[Castle on the Sea]], [[Hydra Island]], or near [[Mansion (Third Sea)|Mansion]], the user may be teleported to the [[Third Sea|third sea]] [[portals]], causing them to go back and forth between islands if they have access.
** There is also a very rare chance the user will not be teleported back and will be stranded at [[sea]].
** Sometimes, the fruit's icon does not show in the [[inventory]]. (Fixed) 
** Although Z's skill (Transformed and Blazing Version) is known for having a ridiculous hit rate, using this skill very close to the opponent (precisely from up to down) can almost one-hit kill any player, as its damage is absurdly broken. It is probably why the move functions in such a unique manner.
*Despite not being entirely related, Werewolf seems to be more parallel to [[Yeti]], both being mythical, wild beasts.
*The Werewolf skin had a tag named "Feral". This was available before the configurator update.

